  "answer": "### Short Answer\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 84 of the NIRC, the estate tax is imposed on the transfer of the net estate of a decedent. The TRAIN law simplified the estate tax structure by establishing a single rate of 6% for estates valued above the threshold of ₱5,000,000, thereby eliminating the previous graduated rates.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis means that for estates with a gross value exceeding ₱5,000,000, the estate tax liability will be calculated at a uniform rate of 6% on the amount above this threshold. Estates valued at ₱5,000,000 or less are exempt from estate tax, which provides significant relief for smaller estates and simplifies the tax compliance process for executors and heirs.",
